---
/**
 * Trailing amber period — the e-ink-paper accent that appears at the end
 * of every primary title on the mobile app (e.g. "Stronger.", "Squat.",
 * "Today."). Inherits the surrounding font-family / size / weight so it
 * sits inline with the heading; just paints the `.` in `--amber`.
 *
 * The amber token (#8E5345) is the only non-ink/non-paper color in the
 * design system. Using it sparingly — one period per page-defining
 * heading — keeps the site visually anchored to the app.
 */
---

<span class="accent-dot" aria-hidden="true">.</span>

<style>
  .accent-dot {
    color: var(--amber);
    /* Pull the period a hair tighter against the preceding word so it
       reads as part of the title, not a stray glyph. */
    margin-left: -0.04em;
  }
</style>
